---
/**
 * The SMI minisite (/smi): SMART Measuring Instruments — physical
 * instruments that provide a SMART digital twin for access and
 * certification. Style: the OIML SMART writing guide.
 */
const aspects = [
  { name: 'The twin interface', desc: 'The instrument serves a structured endpoint: its identity, its characteristics, its state, and its behavior, readable by the platform.' },
  { name: 'The governed projection', desc: 'The SMART Recommendation declares which aspects of the twin it governs. The platform reads the projection, never the vendor’s internals.' },
  { name: 'The evidence stream', desc: 'Probes and verdicts are recorded as they happen. Compliance becomes a continuous record, not an episodic report.' },
]
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>SMART Measuring Instruments — OIML SMART</title>
    <meta name="description" content="OIML SMART Measuring Instruments (OIML SMI) — physical measuring instruments that provide a SMART digital twin for access and certification." />
    <style>
      :root {
        --paper: #faf7f2; --ink: #1a2332; --ink-soft: #4a5568; --accent: #004996;
        --rule: #d9d4c7; --paper-soft: #f3efe7;
      }
      @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
        :root { --paper: #14181f; --ink: #e8e6e1; --ink-soft: #a8b0bc; --accent: #6ba3e8; --rule: #2c3542; --paper-soft: #1c222c; }
      }
      * { box-sizing: border-box; }
      body { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font-family: Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif; line-height: 1.6; }
      main { max-width: 56rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 4rem 1.5rem 6rem; }
      h1 { font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.25rem); font-weight: 500; letter-spacing: -0.025em; line-height: 1.05; margin: 1.5rem 0 1rem; }
      h2 { font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem; }
      p { color: var(--ink-soft); max-width: 42rem; }
      .lede { font-size: 1.125rem; }
      .brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.75rem; text-decoration: none; color: var(--ink); font-size: 0.9375rem; }
      .brand:hover { color: var(--accent); }
      ul { color: var(--ink-soft); }
      li { margin: 0.375rem 0; }
      a { color: var(--accent); }
      footer { margin-top: 4rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <a class="brand" href="https://www.oimlsmart.org/">← OIML SMART</a>
      <picture>
        <source srcset="/smi/img/components/smi-dark.svg" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)" />
        <img src="/smi/img/components/smi-light.svg" alt="The SMART Measuring Instruments logo." width="140" />
      </picture>
      <h1>SMART Measuring Instruments</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A SMART measuring instrument is a physical instrument that provides a SMART digital twin.
        Certification talks to the instrument itself, through its twin: the instrument is the API.
      </p>

      <h2>Purpose</h2>
      <p>
        Certification today reads an instrument through paper: declarations, photographs, and manual
        test records. A SMART measuring instrument answers directly. Its digital twin serves the
        instrument's identity, characteristics, state, and behavior in a structured form the platform
        can query, test, and record. The physical instrument stays the authority; the twin is its
        faithful, live representation.
      </p>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <ul>
        {aspects.map(a => (
          <li><strong>{a.name}.</strong> {a.desc}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <h2>The twin certification program</h2>
      <p>
        A twin must be certified before the platform trusts it: the promise that the twin accurately
        reflects the physical instrument is itself assessed and signed. The twin certification
        program defines that assessment, so a certified twin can stand in for the instrument in
        certification and in continuous compliance monitoring.
      </p>

      <h2>Continuous compliance</h2>
      <p>
        Once certified, the instrument reports through its twin for the whole of its service life.
        The platform monitors the stream against the Recommendation's constraints and re-judges
        compliance when the evidence changes. Periodic re-verification becomes a standing record
        rather than a recurring interruption.
      </p>

      <footer>
        Part of <a href="https://www.oimlsmart.org/">OIML SMART</a>. Developed under the OIML SMART program by Ribose.
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
